I've no specific ring strategy, but some steps I do are; BUC-ID,
put on non-cursed ones to detect levitation, protection, conflict,
regeneration, etc., then price ID to find out the ones worth 300
Zorkmids, check them out at teleport traps (don't wear them too
long because of polymorph), wear some of the other rings to find
out what might be warning or searching, scroll-ID the other rings
as soon as possible. If the rings I mentioned above are amongst
them I wear them; poison resistance is crucial, searching and
warning helps to avoid critical situations, a random resistance
ring (even if yet unidentified) will reduce the overall risk from
a winter wolf or a gnome with a wand of cold or fire, and stealth
or invisibility will help me doing my business mostly undisturbed.
 From my log files I see that I wear very often free action, and, for
example, a +5 ring of gain constitution, two +2 rings of increase
damage, fire resistance, searching, or regeneration, just to name
a few.

